-- title:
--   Augmentation coinvariants: vanishing equals membership in ι(I_G)M
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ and $A$ be commutative rings with $A$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, let $G$ be a finite commutative group, and let $\iota \colon \mathcal{O}[G] \to A$ be a homomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, where $\mathcal{O}[G]$ is the monoid algebra `MonoidAlgebra 𝒪 G`. Let `Mn` be an additive commutative group carrying module structures over $A$, over $\mathcal{O}[G]$ and over $\mathcal{O}$, the $\mathcal{O}$-action being compatible with the $\mathcal{O}[G]$-action by a scalar-tower assumption, and assume that the $\mathcal{O}[G]$-action is obtained from the $A$-action through $\iota$, i.e. $c \cdot x = \iota(c) \cdot x$ for all $c \in \mathcal{O}[G]$ and $x \in$ `Mn`. Write $I_G$ for the kernel of the counit algebra map `Bialgebra.counitAlgHom 𝒪 (MonoidAlgebra 𝒪 G)`, that is, the augmentation ideal of $\mathcal{O}[G]$. Then, for $x \in$ `Mn`, the class of $x$ in the quotient of `Mn` by the $\mathcal{O}[G]$-submodule $I_G \cdot \top$ is zero if and only if $x$ lies in the $A$-submodule $(\iota_* I_G) \cdot \top$, where $\iota_* I_G$ denotes the ideal of $A$ generated by $\iota(I_G)$.
--
--   This identifies the $G$-coinvariant quotient `Mn` $/ I_G\,$`Mn` of a module over a finite group algebra with the quotient by the $A$-submodule generated by the image of the augmentation ideal, the two submodules being generated by the same elements $\iota(c)y$ with $c \in I_G$. It is used in the assembly of Taylor–Wiles patching data, where the coinvariant description of the Taylor–Wiles modules must be matched with a condition formulated in terms of an ideal of $A$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MonoidAlgebra_quotient_mk_eq_zero_iff_mem_map_augmentation_smul_top.lean

